VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the model to save it in the configuration file. It created its own to-do list to do so and enabled this archive chats plugin over here. A few final things about this harness before we wrap up. It has some common slash'

[06:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'commands you\'d expect like go and compact. You can also activate skills with slash commands and skills like other harnesses can be installed through for cells skills.sh and will be picked up here. You can also create your own'

[06:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'custom agent presets using creator mode. And this harness has a feature I haven\'t seen from many other harnesses, which is the ability to change the enter busy behavior. So, it can either be a queue, which means when a model is processing a'

[07:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'response, you can type in another prompt and it will wait for that previous prompt to finish before working on it. Or it could be a steer, which means it will interrupt the previous prompt to listen to your current prompt. But you can toggle this behavior while prompting'

[07:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'by pressing command or control enter instead of pressing just enter. So, that\'s a quick overview of the Deep Sea harness and how to use it with Fire Cru. I would say it\'s a great start, but there are a few things about the harness'

[07:31] [scene:talk]
